if you're an artist or an entrepreneur  and you're having a hard time telling  your story I'm going to share with you  why it's so important on this video and  how to do it hi I'm Evan Carmichael  I believe in entrepreneurs and I  recently got a question from one of my  YouTube subscribers love you guys  Sarah who wrote in the say I'm a  beginner at painting I'm not very public  about it yet and I'm not really  interested in being public because  everyone seems to have 500 questions do  people really have to know the biography  of a painter's life what if their life  was a bad life I'm frustrated because I  hesitate when I cite asking for my bio  so I leave a blank the main reason I  started painting is just because as a  writer I still feel as if I have no  voice but when I paint that feel freedom  I always heard a painting is worth a  thousand words and they're right but I  don't think people should know about  someone's crappy past any advice would  be good is it okay to leave a blank or  can I type up a short version of the  happy moments Sarah this is a fantastic  question and I feel your pain in writing  it and the frustration that you feel and  that you want your business to be  successful and you feel like the know  the Bayeux is an important part of it  you don't know what to put in there the  reason why I bio is so important is  because it helps people make a personal  connection to you but people like buying  from entrepreneurs because they feel  like they're buying from that person and  not just buying from a company and your  story can make the difference between  somebody wanted to buy your art and  somebody just passing it over an example  is a buddy of mine fan of the channel  Pete Elvidge who is a pixel artist and  he creates pixel artwork and he did one  of me as being a Minecraft character and  what's great about Pete is not  necessarily his art skills right he's  getting better he wants to have more  shows he wants to get more sales as his  technique still needs to be refined but  it's his story  what makes Pete greatest he's almost  blind so here's his artist who's making  art which is very visual right and he's  completely blind in one eye and almost  completely blind in the other eye and he  uses that remaining vision that he has  to create pixel art and so even though I  think his art could be better and he's  getting better at  technique and training and working on it  I'm interested in him because of his  story that's what your story does it  helps people connect the art to you now  I think one of the things you have to  get past is you only need to tell the  positive happy moments in your life if  you look at a lot of artist lives  they're not fantastic and some of the  greatest art whether it's paintings or  music or poems came out of periods in  their lives of severe depression anger  upsetness and they funneled that energy  into their art you don't have to just  tell all the good stuff what people want  to know is what went into this artwork  who are you and why are you making these  paintings even being honest in your bio  and saying things that you come alive  when you're painting and you're not  great at writing is an honest truthful  statement that will help make people  connect to you so I'd start with  thinking about why you love painting  write it down and try to get a few  sentences out there about your passion  for painting then I think about how it  makes you feel how does it make you come  alive what stresses that relief from  your life if for example the rest of the  world kind of stresses you out and and  you don't feel like you belong and  painting is the only thing that makes  you come alive then right that put that  down in there right I want to feel that  emotional connection to you you can  write about some of your favorite pieces  the ones that really mean something to  you and how you came up with the  inspiration for them you could talk  about your friends and your family and  how you got into it and if they support  you or if they don't support you and how  you continue to persevere regardless  people don't want to just hear the story  about how great things are do you want  to hear the struggle they want to be  able to relate to you and see themselves  in you nobody has a perfect life and if  that's the goods that you're selling  then it's not going to be authentic and  you'll actually lose people to people  who you watch on youtube or read their  BIOS and really follow other ones who  are honest and authentic and vulnerable  and willing to share that because it  opens them up and allows people to  connect with them on a much deeper level  and that's what you want whether you're  an artist or a regular entrepreneur you  want people to feel connected to you and  what you're doing and make it feel like  they're a part of  your story and your journey and they  want to see where you go with it if  after all that you're still super  private and don't want that information  to get out there then what I'd suggest  is using an alias tell your story in a  way that nobody could pinpoint it that  it being actually you but also getting  it out there on their fake name so that  people can feel like they're connected  to the artist the other side benefit  that I think about when I help share my  story is that it could serve as an  inspiration to others if for example you  feel lost in the regular world and art  helps you escape that and makes you feel  happy that could be a solution for  somebody else who is going through the  same thing in their life they might feel  totally lost and helpless and have  nobody in their life to guide them and  by reading your bio and looking at your  art may inspire them to get into art and  to have a happier life having a great  bio and telling your story will help you  get more customers help you have a much  bigger impact help you make more money  and help you have your art to be more  well-known which i think is 